# Restore (0.5.0)
restore = Restore
old-format-row = Older format: made without ACLs and extended attributes
restore-title = Restore the system?
restore-muted = { $date } · { $comment }
restore-body = Puts system files back to this snapshot and restarts twice.
restore-home-section = Home folders
restore-keep-home = Keep my files as they are now
restore-restore-home = Restore them too
restore-lost-for-good = Files changed after { $date } are lost for good.
restore-safety = Take a snapshot of the current system first (recommended)
restore-no-home = Home folders aren't in this snapshot, so they stay as they are.
restore-old-format = Older format: this snapshot was made without ACLs and extended attributes. A few system files may come back without them.
restore-no-apsis = Apsis wasn't installed yet when this snapshot was made, so it will be gone after the restore. Install it again to see how the restore went.
restore-apsis-no-restore = This snapshot has Apsis { $version }. Install this version of Apsis again afterwards to restore again.
restore-apsis-old-settings = This snapshot has an older Apsis ({ $version }) that can't read the current settings. Install this version of Apsis again afterwards.
restore-experimental = Experimental · if it won't start, see "If a restore goes wrong" (README)
refused-title = Can't restore this snapshot
refused-other-installation = It was made on another installation of the system, so its files don't fit this one.
refused-other-installation-do = Pick a snapshot made on this installation.
refused-not-uefi = This computer doesn't start in UEFI mode, which restore needs.
refused-not-kernelstub = Restore works only on Pop!_OS with systemd-boot for now.
refused-boot-partition = The boot partition isn't where Pop!_OS keeps it.
refused-root-filesystem = Restore doesn't support a { $fstype } system disk yet.
refused-root-device = Restore doesn't support the way this system disk is set up yet.
refused-root-device-do = It works on a plain partition and on Pop!_OS's standard encrypted install. Snapshots still work: their files are on the backup disk, under timeshift/snapshots.
refused-split-system = Restore doesn't support a system split over several partitions yet.
refused-this-computer = Restore can't be used on this computer.
refused-this-computer-yet = Restore can't be used on this computer yet.
refused-kernel-incomplete = This snapshot's kernel files are incomplete.
refused-unreadable = This snapshot can't be read: { $reason }.
refused-unreadable-no-info = it has no info.json
refused-unreadable-not-rsync = it isn't an rsync snapshot
refused-unreadable-no-localhost = it has no system files
refused-unreadable-no-exclude-list = it has no exclude.list
refused-pick-another = Pick another snapshot.
refused-pending-update = A system update is waiting for a restart.
refused-pending-update-do = Restart first, then restore.
refused-restore-armed = A restart to restore is already waiting.
refused-restore-armed-do = Restart the computer, or wait for it to time out.
refused-pop-upgrade = A Pop!_OS upgrade is in progress.
refused-pop-upgrade-do = Finish or cancel it first, then restore.
refused-crypttab = The encrypted disks are set up differently from when this snapshot was made.
refused-crypttab-do = Restore needs a snapshot made with the current disk setup.
refused-backup-space = Not enough space on the backup disk for a safety snapshot (needs { $needs }, { $free } free).
refused-backup-space-do = Delete old snapshots, or turn off the safety snapshot.
refused-system-space = Not enough space on the system disk to restore (needs { $needs }, { $free } free).
refused-system-space-do = Free some space, then try again.
refused-boot-space = Not enough space on the boot partition (needs { $needs }, { $free } free).
refused-boot-space-do = Remove an old kernel, then try again.
refused-size-unknown = The restore's size couldn't be measured.
refused-size-unknown-do = Try again. If it happens again, see the README.
refused-boot-files = The boot files on this computer don't match the kernel it started with.
refused-boot-files-do = Install the latest kernel update, restart, then try again.
refused-dropped = The preparation was dropped. Restore again to measure afresh.
close = Close
preparing-checking = Preparing restore · checking the snapshot…
preparing-space = Preparing restore · checking disk space…
preparing-safety = Preparing restore · safety snapshot · { $percent } · { $time } left
