restart-now = Restart now
restarting = Restarting…
restore-cancelled = Restore cancelled
restore-too-old = The preparation is too old. Start the restore again.
restore-gone = The preparation is gone. Start the restore again.
result-done = System restored to { $date }
result-problems-before = Restore finished ·
result-problems-phrase = some files were not restored
result-problems-after = · point here for details
result-problems-other-phrase = a cleanup step failed
result-problems-other-after = · point here for details
result-boot-kept-before = System restored ·
result-boot-kept-phrase = still boots the previous kernel
result-boot-kept-after = · see README
result-boot-broken-before = Restore finished ·
result-boot-broken-phrase = the computer may not start next time
result-boot-broken-after = · read the README before restarting
result-failed-before = Restore
result-failed-phrase = incomplete
result-failed-after = · system partly restored · { $what }
result-what-disk = reconnect the backup disk
result-what-space = free space on the system disk
result-what-readme = see README
result-not-started = The restore didn't start · nothing was changed · { $what }
restore-again = Restore again
result-done-tip = Restored from snapshot { $name }. { $home } Safety snapshot: { $safety }.
result-home-kept = Home folders were kept.
result-home-restored = Home folders were restored too.
result-safety-none = none
result-problems-tip = Restored from snapshot { $name }. { $home } Safety snapshot: { $safety }. What went wrong: { $reason }
result-boot-kept-tip = Restored to { $date }. The boot files couldn't be refreshed, so the computer keeps the ones it had and runs the kernel from before the restore. The next kernel update should set this right. See "If a restore goes wrong" in Apsis's README.
result-boot-broken-tip = Restored to { $date }, but the boot files are not in order and the computer may not start the next time you restart. Before you restart, read "If a restore goes wrong" in Apsis's README. What went wrong: { $reason }
result-failed-tip = Stopped after 3 tries: { $reason }. Reconnect the backup disk and click Restore again, or restore the safety snapshot.
result-failed-tip-no-safety = Stopped after 3 tries: { $reason }. Reconnect the backup disk and click Restore again. No safety snapshot was taken.
